  "article_notes": "86 client-owned dogs with B. rossi (capillary smear, PCR-confirmed) at OVAH; dogs with complicated babesiosis (ARF, cerebral, coagulopathy, icterus/hepatopathy, IMHA, haemoconcentration, ARDS) were excluded, so the severity contrast is within uncomplicated disease. Severity = transfused (more anaemic) vs non-transfused dogs. Samples at presentation (dogs were treated at presentation; timing relative to diminazene not stated) and at Day 1, 3 and 6 after treatment; regression rows cover all days. Outcome did not differ between groups (P = 0.62; 2 deaths in each), not extracted as a marker. Effects of age and of whole blood vs packed cells are not severity comparisons. Per-group serial values are mostly in box plots (Figs 1-9).",
